Investigate this Wazuh alert:

{
  "severity": "high",
  "network_observations": [
    {"ip": "10.40.8.71", "inferred_role": "it_admin_workstation_compromised", "first_seen": "2027-09-22T02:58:42+0200", "last_seen": "2027-09-22T03:09:14+0200", "agent_name": "WS-ADMIN-04.corp.local"}
  ],
  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Initial Access / Valid Accounts", "technique": "T1078.003", "what_happened": "At 2027-09-22 02:58:42 CEST, Event 4624 'An account was successfully logged on' fired on WS-ADMIN-04.corp.local (10.40.8.71) with TargetUserName=admin.local, IpAddress=10.40.8.71, logonType=2 (Interactive — physical console OR RDP via console session at the local-host loopback IP). The 02:58 hour for an interactive logon on an IT admin workstation is outside typical business hours and outside the host's baseline activity profile. The fact that IpAddress = host's own IP (10.40.8.71) and logonType=2 means the session was initiated either physically at the keyboard OR via a console-redirection mechanism (out-of-band card, virtual KVM, or RDP-to-console). admin.local is a local-administrator-class account, NOT a domain account.", "chain_reason": "Windows Security Event 4624 (rule.id 60224, level 12). Baseline-deviation rule flagged: logonType=2 on WS-ADMIN-04 outside 08:00-19:00 + targetUserName=admin.local (privileged local account).", "first_seen": "2027-09-22T02:58:42+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Defense Evasion (AV Tamper — PowerShell Defender API)", "technique": "T1562.001", "what_happened": "At 03:02:18 CEST (~3 min 36 s after the interactive logon), Sysmon Event 1 fired on WS-ADMIN-04 with image=powershell.exe + commandLine='powershell.exe -Command \"Set-MpPreference -DisableRealtimeMonitoring $true -DisableScriptScanning $true -DisableIOAVProtection $true\"' + parentImage=cmd.exe + user=CORP\\admin.local. Set-MpPreference is the Defender configuration cmdlet; the three flags collectively disable: (a) real-time file-system monitoring (RTP), (b) PowerShell script scanning, (c) Inbound Origin AV protection on downloaded content. One second later at 03:02:19, Windows Defender event channel logged Event 5001 'Real-Time Protection is disabled' on the same host — direct cause-effect with the PowerShell tamper.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon Event 1: image=powershell.exe + commandLine contains 'Set-MpPreference' + 'DisableRealtimeMonitoring' + 'DisableScriptScanning' + 'DisableIOAVProtection'. Windows Defender Event 5001 fired within 1 second of the Sysmon command. Diagnostic of programmatic AV-disable via the official Defender PowerShell API, NOT user-driven GUI action.", "first_seen": "2027-09-22T03:02:18+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Defense Evasion (Service Stop — WinDefend)", "technique": "T1562.001 + T1489", "what_happened": "At 03:07:18 CEST (~5 min after the PowerShell tamper), Sysmon Event 1 fired with image=sc.exe + commandLine='sc.exe stop \"WinDefend\"' + parentImage=cmd.exe + user=CORP\\admin.local — the attacker escalated from disabling Defender's RTP via API to STOPPING the Windows Defender service entirely. At the SAME timestamp 03:07:18, Windows Security Event 4719 'System audit policy was changed' fired with SubcategoryGUID={0CCE9210-69AE-11D9-BED3-505054503030} (Logon/Logoff audit subcategory) + AuditPolicyChanges=%%8448 (Success removed) — the attacker simultaneously REMOVED audit logging for Logon/Logoff events to suppress future Event 4624/4625/4634 generation. 3 seconds later at 03:07:21, Windows Security Event 7036 'Service WinDefend entered the stopped state' confirmed the service stop succeeded.", "chain_reason": "Three-event correlation in 3-second window: (a) Sysmon Event 1 image=sc.exe + commandLine '*stop*WinDefend*', (b) Windows Security Event 4719 with SubcategoryGUID Logon/Logoff + AuditPolicyChanges=%%8448 (Success removed), (c) Windows Security Event 7036 service stop confirmation. The combination = deliberate, multi-vector defense-evasion play, not a misconfiguration.", "first_seen": "2027-09-22T03:07:18+0200"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Defense Evasion (EDR Service Stop — Sense)", "technique": "T1562.001", "what_happened": "At 03:07:24 CEST (6 seconds after stopping WinDefend), Sysmon Event 1 fired with image=sc.exe + commandLine='sc.exe stop \"Sense\"' + parentImage=cmd.exe + user=CORP\\admin.local. The 'Sense' service is the Windows Defender Advanced Threat Protection / Defender for Endpoint EDR component. Stopping Sense disables MDE telemetry uploads to the cloud, ASR rule enforcement, and tamper-protection enforcement (when the latter isn't in 'protected' mode). This is the SECOND consecutive defender-component shutdown by the same actor — the AV+EDR layered defense has been deliberately dismantled.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon Event 1: image=sc.exe + commandLine '*stop*Sense*' + parentImage=cmd.exe + user=CORP\\admin.local, 6 seconds after the WinDefend stop. Sequential AV-then-EDR shutdown is the textbook 'flatten endpoint defenses before payload' attacker pattern.", "first_seen": "2027-09-22T03:07:24+0200"},
    {"step": 5, "tactic": "Credential Access (LSASS Memory Dump)", "technique": "T1003.001", "what_happened": "At 03:09:11 CEST (~107 seconds after the EDR shutdown), Sysmon Event 1 fired with image=mimikatz.exe + commandLine='mimikatz.exe sekurlsa::logonpasswords' + parentImage=cmd.exe + user=CORP\\admin.local. The attacker waited ~2 minutes after disabling AV/EDR — enough time for the service-stop to propagate + AV exclusions to take effect + telemetry to drain — then launched mimikatz with the sekurlsa::logonpasswords command (extracts NTLM hashes, Kerberos TGTs, and plaintext passwords from LSASS memory for every interactive logon on the host). 3 seconds later at 03:09:14, Sysmon Event 10 (ProcessAccess) fired with SourceImage=mimikatz.exe + TargetImage=C:\\Windows\\System32\\lsass.exe + GrantedAccess=0x1010 — direct LSASS handle open from mimikatz, confirming the credential dump fired.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon Event 1: image=*mimikatz* + commandLine '*sekurlsa::logonpasswords*' + parentImage=cmd.exe + user=CORP\\admin.local, plus Sysmon Event 10 (ProcessAccess) SourceImage=*mimikatz* + TargetImage=*lsass.exe* + GrantedAccess=0x1010 within 3 seconds. The chain 'AV-disable → EDR-stop → mimikatz LSASS read' is the canonical credential-access TTP that only works after defense evasion succeeds.", "first_seen": "2027-09-22T03:09:11+0200"}
  ],
  "time_window": {"start": "2027-09-22T02:58:42+0200", "end": "2027-09-22T03:09:14+0200"},
